el': {}, 'has_graduated_access': True, 'is_blue_verified': True, 'profile_image_shape': 'Circle', 'legacy': {'can_dm': True, 'can_media_tag': True, 'created_at': 'Mon Mar 04 00:01:50 +0000 2019', 'default_profile': True, 'default_profile_image': False, 'description': 'Ag Policy Fellow and Writer - working to make real food legal again from American farmers and ranchers', 'entities': {'description': {'urls': []}}, 'fast_followers_count': 0, 'favourites_count': 32265, 'followers_count': 18035, 'friends_count': 2540, 'has_custom_timelines': True, 'is_translator': False, 'listed_count': 56, 'location': 'United States', 'media_count': 1924, 'name': 'Breeauna Sagdal', 'normal_followers_count': 18035, 'pinned_tweet_ids_str': ['1708008148861153681'], 'possibly_sensitive': False, 'profile_banner_url': 'https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/1102358449734578176/1697002305', 'profile_image_url_https': 'https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1102359933045989376/Dc-eXj0D_normal.jpg', 'profile_interstitial_type': '', 'screen_name': 'Breeauna9', 'statuses_count': 16358, 'translator_type': 'none', 'verified': False, 'want_retweets': False, 'withheld_in_countries': []}}}}, 'unmention_data': {}, 'edit_control': {'initial_tweet_id': '1879643753503424593', 'edit_control_initial': {'edit_tweet_ids': ['1879643753503424593', '1879644965539614798'], 'editable_until_msecs': '1736980567000', 'is_edit_eligible': True, 'edits_remaining': '4'}}, 'previous_counts': {'bookmark_count': 2, 'favorite_count': 5, 'quote_count': 1, 'reply_count': 0, 'retweet_count': 2}, 'is_translatable': False, 'views': {'count': '18901', 'state': 'EnabledWithCount'}, 'source': '<a href="http://twitter.com/download/android" rel="nofollow">Twitter for Android</a>', 'note_tweet': {'is_expandable': True, 'note_tweet_results': {'result': {'id': 'Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjE4Nzk2NDQ5NjUyMDgyODEwODg=', 'text': '🚨🚨🚨A Coup Da Ta?🚨🚨🚨\n\n@realDailyWire and @JamesOKeefeIII have now confirmed (from various sources) that  Succession orders - published to the Federal Register on Monday, Jan. 13, 2025 (the day before nomination hearings began) - are more than mere hurdles to delay the Trump administration. In fact,  we might be looking at an outright coup.\n\nGoing back to May of 2024, I found it odd that the Office of Personnel Management (OPM) began slowly rearranging scheduled employees - moving Biden\'s politically appointed Senior level Advisors to Schedule A.\n"Schedule A (federal employees) is a special appointing authority that agencies can use to non-competitively appoint individuals, including eligible veterans, and those with a disability." \n\nKeeping this in the back of my mind, I immediately recognized Monday\'s blitzkrieg of rule changes as being part of a larger plot.  However,  given that this was implemented after an Executive Order, I still doubted my instincts given the Congressional Review Act, and @WCdispatch_\npromised me I was overreacting...\n\nHowever, as it turns out, the Biden administration requested an August 29, 2024 Congressional Research Council report which indicates there are Three Exemptions to the CRA/types of administrative rule changes that Congress CAN NOT claw back: \n\n"The CRA excludes three types of actions from this definition (5 U.S.C. §804(3)):\n1. Rules of particular applicability;\n2. Rules relating to agency management or personnel; and\n3. Rules of agency organization, procedure, or practice that do\nnot substantially affect the rights and obligations of non-agency \nparties.\n\nThus, even IF Trump revokes the Executive Order (Jan. 3, 2025) which ordered the new line of succession, the Biden administration has already moved their people into place! \n\nMeaning:\n1. Congress doesn\'t appear to have authority to overturn these new rule changes as they\'re related to personnel AND rules of agency organization;\n2. Employees reordered under Schedule A can sue if fired, and  they\'re much harder to get rid of;\n3. These are the very employees that would be responsible for implementing Trump\'s E.O. revocation orders, and that\'s not going to happen so long as they\'re in place. \n\nI\'m now absolutely convinced that this isn\'t merely a hurdle but may potentially be an actual Coup de ta. And why not? Trump has promised to cut jobs and remove the centralized authority of the administrative state!\n\nDid anyone really expect this fascist, unlawful structure to just give up its power? \n\nThe question is what the Trump administration plans to do,  and so far, it doesn\'t look like a solid plan even exists. \n\nCRS report on exemptions to the CRA\nhttps://t.co/wWHXKMAgAL', 'entity_set': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'urls': [{'display_url': 'crsreports.congress.gov/product/pdf/IF…', 'expanded_url': 'https://crsreports.congress.gov/product/pdf/IF/IF10023', 'url': 'https://t.co/wWHXKMAgAL', 'indices': [2678, 2701]}], 'user_mentions': [{'id_str': '4081106480', 'name': 'Daily Wire', 'screen_name': 'realDailyWire', 'indices': [21, 35]}, {'id_str': '16989178', 'name': "James O'Keefe", 'screen_name': 'JamesOKeefeIII', 'indices': [40, 55]}, {'id_str': '1520041705076101122', 'name': 'Walter Curt', 'screen_name': 'WCdispatch_', 'indices': [1010, 1022]}]}, 'richtext': {'richtext_tags': []}}}}, 'quotedRefResult': {'result': {'__typename': 'Tweet', 'rest_id': '1879029351590588744'}}, 'legacy': {'bookmark_count': 54, 'bookmarked': False, 'created_at': 'Wed Jan 15 21:40:56 +0000 2025', 'conversation_id_str': '1879644965539614798', 'display_text_range': [0, 273], 'entities': {'hashtags': [], 'media': [{'display_url': 'pic.x.com/NZaDMbYPI5', 'expanded_url': 'https://x.com/Breeauna9/status/1879644965539614798/photo/1', 'id_str': '1879643747283054592', 'indices': [274, 297], 'media_key': '3_1879643747283054592', 'media_url_https': 'https://pbs.twimg.com/media/GhXWB4UXMAAz7HE.jpg', 'type': 'photo', 'url': 'https://t.co/NZaDMbYPI5', 'ext_media_availability': {'status': 'Available'}, 'features': {'large': {'faces': [{'x': 498, 'y': 663, 'h': 84, 'w